course: dictionary
lesson: 316
title: One name, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Some words are names, and one name can have more than one meaning. Andromeda is a proper noun, so it always starts with a capital letter. Context tells you which meaning is meant. «In autumn the Great Square of Pegasus rises in the east, and from its corner a line of stars leads to Andromeda.» The stars and the sky show that this is about space, so Andromeda means a galaxy or a group of stars.
explain: Look for clues in the words after the name. «The Andromeda Galaxy, about 2.5 million light years away, is the farthest thing most people can see with the naked eye.» The word Galaxy and the huge distance tell you this is a galaxy, far, far away in space.
explain: Stories give different clues. In old Greek myths, Andromeda is a princess saved by a hero. When you meet a name, ask: is this a person, a place or a thing? Let the words around it decide.
fact: Andromeda is a proper noun, so it begins with a capital letter.
fact: The Andromeda Galaxy is the nearest large galaxy to our own galaxy, the Milky Way.
fact: The Andromeda Galaxy is a spiral galaxy made of hundreds of billions of stars.
fact: Andromeda is also a constellation, which means a group of stars in the night sky.
fact: In old Greek myths, Andromeda was a princess saved from a sea monster by the hero Perseus.
exercise: «In autumn the Great Square of Pegasus rises in the east, and from its corner a line of stars leads to Andromeda.» In this sentence, what is Andromeda? | *A group of stars in the night sky | A sea monster | A kind of farm animal | A bright red fruit
exercise: «The Andromeda Galaxy, about 2.5 million light years away, is the farthest thing most people can see with the naked eye.» What is the Andromeda Galaxy? | A town in Greece | A princess who lived long ago | A kind of sea monster | *A huge galaxy far away, made of stars
exercise: In the old Greek myth, who saved the princess Andromeda? | *The hero Perseus | A sea monster | The Milky Way | A telescope
test: What is the nearest large galaxy to our own galaxy, the Milky Way? | Our own galaxy | The Sun | *Andromeda | The Moon
test: «A line of stars leads to Andromeda.» Which clue shows Andromeda is in the sky? | *A line of stars | A sea monster | A hero | A princess
exam: «The Andromeda Galaxy, about 2.5 million light years away, is the farthest thing most people can see with the naked eye.» In this sentence, what is the best meaning of Andromeda Galaxy? | A dark cloud on the ground | The town where the hero Perseus was born | A princess in a Greek myth | *A galaxy far, far away, made of hundreds of billions of stars
